sam (docs): FYI I'm opening a docs PR (#5678) to update SDK snippets: replace old page-token examples with continuation-token/resume patterns, and add clearer streaming retry guidance across Py/TS/Go. Need quick sanity checks and a lint pass.

violet (sdk): Nice. Do you want the TS example to show explicit reconnect logic (cursor write-back) or just a note to use the SDK helper?

sam (docs): Show explicit reconnect + cursor write-back so readers understand the low-level flow; add a pointer to the helper API in a follow-up note.

raj (eng): Also we should include a short paragraph about cost: full restarts can produce duplicate tokens and double-bill in some cases. Recommend idempotency keys or server offsets where available.

violet (sdk): Draft snippets below. Please flag anything that will trip the snippets-lint harness.

violet (sdk): Python async continuation example:
```python
# from rwd import Client
# client = Client()  # reuse per process
async def stream_with_continuation(prompt):
    cont = load_continuation_token()  # may be None
    try:
        async for ev in client.responses.stream(model='rwd/sm-1', input=prompt, continuation_token=cont):
            if ev.type == 'delta':
                print(ev.text, end='')
            elif ev.type == 'continuation':
                save_continuation(ev.token)
    except TransientError:
        # prefer resuming from saved continuation token; avoid naive full restart
        await backoff_and_resume(prompt)
```

sam (docs): Good. Add a one-line security caveat about not storing raw user secrets in continuation storage.

violet (sdk): TS reconnect + continuation pattern:
```ts
// assume client is initialized once for the app
let continuation = await readContinuation();
while (true) {
  const stream = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'rwd/sm-1', input: text, continuation });
  for await (const e of stream) {
    if (e.type === 'delta') process.stdout.write(e.text);
    if (e.type === 'continuation') { continuation = e.token; await writeContinuation(continuation); }
  }
  // exit after clean completion, or loop to reconnect if necessary
  break;
}
```

raj (eng): For Go services keep the example idiomatic and show iterator.Err() at the end. Also mention Dedicated customers can use server-side offsets for stronger guarantees.

violet (sdk): Go iterator example (pseudo-types):
```go
it := client.StreamResponses(ctx, &Request{Model: "rwd/sm-1", Input: input, Continuation: saved})
for it.Next() {
  ev := it.Event()
  switch ev.Type {
  case "delta": fmt.Print(ev.Text)
  case "continuation": persistContinuation(ev.Token)
  }
}
if err := it.Err(); err != nil { log.Printf("stream error: %v", err) }
```

sam (docs): I'll also add a docs-only recommended retry policy block (pseudo-config) so we don't accidentally ship unsafe code examples: 
```
max_retries: 3
initial_backoff_ms: 150
backoff_factor: 2
resume_on_continuation: true
avoid_full_restart_unless_idempotent: true
```

